# Astra-CISO v2.0 — Cursor Rules
# Architecture context for AI-assisted development

## Platform Overview
- CISO command center built on ZTAIP (Zero Trust AI Platform) architecture
- Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript 5, Prisma 7, SQLite, Zustand
- Dark hacker theme (Bloomberg Terminal aesthetic) — never use light backgrounds
- 8 modules, 11 sidebar items, tab-based internal navigation

## Modules (8 total)
1. Command Center — Overview, Executive Brief, Reports & Board Deck
2. Decision Center — Decisions, Action Queue
3. Strategy & OKRs — OKRs, Defense Matrix, KPI Dashboard, Program Tracker
4. Governance & Risk — Compliance, Risk Register, Policy Engine, Audit Logs, Evidence Vault
5. Vendor Risk — Quick Answer, Knowledge Transfer, Knowledge Base, CAIQ Review, Vendor Registry
6. Incidents — Active Incidents, War Room, Tabletop Exercises
7. Intelligence — Threat Briefing, World Monitor, Attack Surface, Signal Intelligence, Infrastructure, Military & Maritime, Live Feeds, Ransomware
8. AppSec — Vulnerability Feed, SAST Scanner, Remediation Tracking

## Sidebar Items (11)
Command Center, Decision Center, Strategy & OKRs, Governance & Risk, Vendor Risk, Incidents, Intelligence, AppSec, Settings, Help, Roadmap

## Architecture Patterns
- ZTAIP: Zero Trust AI Platform — never trust, always verify
- Circuit Breaker: CLOSED → OPEN → HALF_OPEN per AI provider and intel API
- Dynamic Autonomy Router: AUTONOMOUS / SUPERVISED / MANUAL
- Immutable Audit Fabric: append-only AuditLog, never update/delete

## AI Providers (multi-provider)
- Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, Ollama (local)
- Always use circuit breaker per provider
- AI Economics: track tokens, cost, queries

## Intelligence Module Patterns
### API Clients (src/lib/intelligence/clients/)
- All clients use circuit breaker pattern
- All clients cache with TTL (never uncached API calls)
- Graceful degradation: return cached data or empty state on failure

### Shodan
- Rate limit: 1 request/second (free tier)
- Cache: host lookups 24h, search 1h
- All lookups logged to audit trail

### Abuse.ch
- ThreatFox: JSON POST to threatfox-api.abuse.ch
- URLhaus: Form-encoded POST to urlhaus-api.abuse.ch (NOT JSON)
- MalwareBazaar: JSON POST to mb-api.abuse.ch
- No API key needed for any Abuse.ch service

### Data Layers (World Monitor)
- Static layers: load from src/data/intelligence/*.json (always available)
- API-fed layers: show "Configure in Settings" if key missing
- All layers toggleable in LayerControlPanel

## Dark Theme Colors
- Background: #050508
- Card BG: rgba(8,12,24,0.85)
- Card Border: rgba(56,189,248,0.06)
- Primary accent: #38bdf8
- Success: #4ade80
- Warning: #fbbf24
- Critical: #ef4444

## Typography
- JetBrains Mono — numbers, metrics, KPIs (bold, colored)
- DM Sans — labels, descriptions, body text

## Component Organization
- src/components/command/ — Command Center widgets
- src/components/intelligence/ — Intelligence components
- src/components/intelligence/world-monitor/ — World Monitor map components
- src/components/intelligence/tabs/ — Intelligence tab wrappers

## Code Conventions
- TypeScript strict mode, no `any` types
- Zod validation at all API boundaries
- React Server Components by default, 'use client' only when needed
- Prisma for all persistent data (never localStorage for business data)
- Zustand for UI state only (sidebar collapse, theme, active tab)
- @/ path alias for imports

## Database
- SQLite via Prisma 7
- 17 models (see prisma/schema.prisma)
- Key models: KnowledgeEntry (1000+ entries), AttackSurfaceScan, AuditLog

## Deleted Features (DO NOT reference or recreate)
- Wargames module (replaced by Tabletop Exercises)
- Budget module
- Infrastructure placeholder
- Privacy placeholder
- Network telemetry widget
- OpenClaw agent (replaced by native AI)
- MISP integration (replaced by Abuse.ch)
- Light/purple theme (replaced by dark hacker theme)
- Docker-based threat intel stack (replaced by cloud APIs)
- 20-item sidebar (now 11 items)
